Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?iOS:=20fix=20cross-core=20icache=20staleness=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20NtFlushInstructionCache=20+=20fast-write=20ON?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause of the Thumper-desktop ILL crashes: FEX_IOS_HOST flushed
cross-modified code with inline dc/ic asm, which broadcasts cache
maintenance but cannot force the remote core's required ISB (needs the
kernel IPI that FlushInstructionCache/sys_icache_invalidate provide).
A core entering a freshly-published block through stale icache lines
(still NOP prefill) slid into the block tail — every crash pc was
exactly 64-byte cache-line aligned. Trap-mode's fault-emulated writes
(~300K mach exceptions per compile storm) widened the window ~1000x.

- JIT.cpp: IOSFlushOneInstr + whole-block flush → NtFlushInstructionCache
- Module.cpp: fast-write re-enabled (WriteOffset = real RX→RW delta),
  per the 2026-07-03 TODO; if the old msvcp140/steam_api64 fast-write
  crashes return, revert WriteOffset to 0 but keep the NtFlush.
- Core.cpp/JIT.cpp: [fex-entry]/[fex-link] publication validation probes
  (silent in healthy runs; exonerated the compile path during diagnosis)

Verified: Thumper windowed-desktop gameplay 200+ FPS, emulated-STR count
294K → 4, launch-to-splash visibly faster, multiple regression-free runs.

